window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"akshan","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Skill","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"His spike — Aureate Rush (E) lands on a 10s cooldown before Heroic Swing is charged, and there is no escape after. Respect the wave."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Comeuppance finally gives you a fair fight, but the channel is interruptible — cast it from cover or when his gap-close is down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His duel spike: sustain and tankiness beat your lethality poke flat. A straight 1v1 is unwinnable — chip and kite only."},{"when":"Late","text":"He owns the sidelane and punishes your revive roams with towers. Pick revives that trade up or don't leave at all."}],"wants":{"you":["Max-range poke, never brawl","Comeuppance from safety","Map plays over sidelane duels"],"foe":["E onto you at level 2","Straight duels at first item","Towers while you roam to revive"]},"early":"Open even — poke from max range while he farms outside grapple reach. The lane turns at level 2: Aureate Rush (E) is a 10s dash that arrives before Heroic Swing is charged. Worse is Dreaded Return (W), an 850-range stab that PULLS you in, so your own Q range is not safe ground. Hug turret and survive 2-5.","mid":"Level 6 finally gives you a fair fight — Comeuppance adds real burst — but the channel is interruptible, and The Darkin Glaive (Q) recasts into a knockup that cuts it, so open only once his 10s gap-close is spent. Do not straight-duel at first item; Q and R both heal him through your poke. Chip, kite, buy anti-heal.","late":"He wins the sidelane: two-plus items he out-pressures you and takes towers whenever you roam to revive. His own passive revives him at full Determination, so one kill may not settle it. Bring Grievous Wounds for the Q and R heals, shove before you leave, and poke him down before he reaches your line.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you poke from range and he farms safely outside grapple threat; nobody can force anything yet.","Zaahen spikes at 2: Aureate Rush (E) is a 10s dash that lands before Heroic Swing is charged, and once he is on you there is no escape.","Level 3 is his — Dreaded Return (W) pulls you from 850, so your own Q range sits inside his engage, not outside it.","Levels 4-5 stay Zaahen's: he punishes every cooldown you burn and your squishy frame can't trade back into his sustain.","At 6 it's even — Comeuppance adds burst he must respect, but it's an interruptible channel he can cut, so cast it from safety.","First item is his: The Darkin Glaive and Grim Deliverance both heal him through your poke. Refuse the 1v1, chip, buy anti-heal.","Two-plus items he owns the sidelane, out-pressuring you and taking towers whenever you roam to revive. Trade map pressure carefully or he grinds you down."]});
