window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"akshan","b":"masteryi","win":["Akshan","Akshan","Akshan","Skill","Skill","Master Yi","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Full kiting poke comes online with Heroic Swing — he cannot punish a single thing you do pre-item."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Both ults spike at once — Highlander (85s) is slow-immune, so range is your answer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His DPS spike: Wuju Style's true damage out-DPSes you the moment he sticks. Swing out before he closes."},{"when":"Late","text":"Highlander resets shred a squishy marksman — win with range, vision and teammates, never the 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Free poke he can't answer","Shield up before trades","Kiting room with walls"],"foe":["Even farm to first item","Alpha Strike your R","Reset chains off your backline"]},"early":"Free poke phase — take it. Your double-hit Q chips him every time he shows, your passive shield wins the level 2 exchanges, and level 3's kite pattern means he can't punish you. Poke the moment Alpha Strike (20s at rank 1) is spent — his basic attacks shorten it, so count his autos, not seconds.","mid":"By 4 his Wuju points even the trades and 6 puts both ults on the table. He is untargetable through Alpha Strike, so a Comeuppance fired as he commits is lost — bait the dash, then channel. The moment his first item finishes, stop taking honest fights: Meditate heals your chip back, so buy Grievous Wounds and swing out early.","late":"Late is his in any stuck fight — Highlander refunds his cooldowns on takedowns and its slow immunity means kiting items don't hold him. Never let him start the fight: poke him entering lanes, swing over walls the moment he flashes intent, and in teamfights stand behind your frontline and let Comeuppance and revives work.","whys":["Akshan owns level 1 — the double-hit Q pokes him twice per trade and he has no way to answer back.","Level 2 stays yours: your passive shield-and-burst pattern wins every short exchange he takes.","Level 3 is yours outright — full kiting poke with Heroic Swing, and he still has nothing to punish you with.","By 4 his Wuju Style points bring it to even — trades are honest now, so pick them on Alpha Strike's 20s down.","Level 6 is a skill stage: Highlander (85s) makes him slow-immune, so the fight goes to whoever spends it better.","Master Yi takes first item: Wuju true damage out-DPSes you the moment he sticks. Kite or die — no standing fights.","Late is his — Highlander resets and true damage shred your squishy frame. You win with range, vision and teammates, never with a 1v1."]});
